Testing on sqrt(pi)1_A keeps the essential q^2: I_pi<=lambda1 q^2+lambda2 q(1-q)+sqrt(Dd1)q. A6 supplies one common L0 with lambda2<=1-3G/4 and d1+sqrt(Bd1)<=G/8. For0<q<=1/2, q^2<=q and1-q>=1/2 then give I_pi<=(1-G/4)q. Arbitrarily small q is allowed here only because this is the auxiliary coercivity step; the subsequent absolute actual comparison still loses relative control there.

