If q>=64B epsilon^2/c^2, the two relative errors are at most c/4 and c^2/64<=c/64. Thus J/q>=47c/64>=c/2=G/8. Since64B/c^2=1024B/G^2, expanding epsilon^2 gives1024B^3 eta^(2(k+1))/G^2. Strict conductance<G/8 implies strict mass below that threshold. A threshold above1/2 simply gives an empty exclusion interval in that dimension. The floor supplies b mu(A)<=q.
