OBJECTIONS AND REMAINING LIMITS
No unresolved mathematical objection blocks the bounded theorem set. Tested attacks included reversed reciprocal Cauchy, insufficient tail exponents, treating real degree projections as Lp contractions, lost normalization, falsely identifying an auxiliary Perron vector, an unpaid growing-degree cutoff, omitting a cross block, replacing a global entropy modulus by its local coefficient, lost q^2 or threshold powers, reversed Cheeger direction, numerator-versus-ratio confusion, lost atom factors, rho^3 errors, and small-mass/cardinality conflation. The checks above resolve these within the actual hypotheses.
Two nonblocking clarity observations are retained without editing the frozen source. First, the model's general matching definition relies on the standard integer meaning of degree-k order, whereas the counterexample theorem explicitly says integer. A future editorial edition may explicitly say integer k in the model to make that shared convention immediate; this verdict does not certify a real-k reinterpretation of eta^(k+1). Second, the counterexample proof opens 'For sufficiently large L' although its block formula is valid for every L with k_L+1<=L and the other dimensions have an explicit fallback. Writing that latter phrase directly would expose the all-L definition more cleanly. The existing proof and exact retained344 source supply that definition; no asymptotic or admissibility step fails.
The final support paragraph still says 'even an accepted version of this section'. This is a conditional scope warning left from preparation, not a mathematical assumption or a claim that346 lacks its retained acceptance. The current review history is explained elsewhere. It need not trigger a mathematical rewrite during this freeze.
The main open limitations are substantive: no actual critical r moment/tail bound, no full operator perturbation, no all-rho support theorem, no relative capacity control below the mass threshold, no admissible collapsing family, no numerical evaluation of inherited alpha/L0, no endpoint-uniform limit and no novelty clearance. The two restrictions do not cover all remaining cuts. ORIGINAL GLOBAL STATIONARY GAP REMAINS OPEN.

